This Privacy Policy governs the collection, processing, and protection of personal data across all services offered by MyJudicial, including:

• Citizen and business client directory browsing, legal search, and map-based advocate discovery;
• Client intake wizard and AI-assisted case triage;
• Appointment scheduling, consultation management, and LiveKit encrypted video conferencing;
• Secure escrow custody for consultation fee deposits and releases;
• Encrypted document storage in the MyJudicial legal vault (OCI Object Storage);
• Verified advocate profile hosting, onboarding, and compliance credentialing.

Scope Boundary: This policy applies strictly to the technical platform and infrastructure managed by MyJudicial. When you retain an advocate for legal representation in court or formal legal advisory, that advocate acts as an independent professional bound by statutory legal professional privilege, the Rwanda Bar Association Code of Conduct, and their own professional secrecy duties.

NO Automated Legal Decisions: MyJudicial does NOT subject users to automated decision-making processes that produce legal effects or similarly significant consequences (such as automated rejection of service, automated account termination, or automated fee liability).

Transparent Multi-Factor Ranking Logic: When clients search for legal experts, our recommendation engine orders search results using an objective, multi-factor algorithm based on:

1. Semantic Relevance (40%): Alignment between the user's matter description and the advocate's verified practice profile;
2. Advocate Rating (25%): Historical review ratings submitted by verified clients from completed consultations;
3. Budget Fit (15%): Comparison between the advocate's published flat consultation rate and the client's declared budget;
4. Verified Review Volume (10%): Total number of completed client reviews;
5. Professional Experience (5%): Documented years of practice since Bar admission;
6. Specialty Match (5%): Direct alignment with the advocate's designated primary legal specialty.

User Autonomy: This ranking score is purely a sorting mechanism for discoverability. Clients retain complete discretion to filter, compare, and select any registered advocate regardless of ranking order.

Infrastructure Location: To guarantee enterprise resilience, fault tolerance, and scalable performance, MyJudicial utilizes reputable global cloud providers whose server infrastructure is situated outside the Republic of Rwanda:

• Core Database & Authentication: Supabase / Amazon Web Services (AWS) data centers located in the European Union and the United States;
• Encrypted Document Vault: Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI) Object Storage facilities located in the United States and the European Union;
• Video Consultation Streaming: LiveKit Cloud infrastructure operating across global edge facilities;
• Transactional Email & SMS Delivery: Brevo data centers located in the European Union;
• Cache Storage: Upstash Redis clusters located in the European Union and the United States.

Statutory Compliance: In accordance with Articles 40, 41, and 42 of Rwanda Law No. 058/2021, transfers of personal data outside Rwanda are conducted under robust legal safeguards, including comprehensive Data Processing Agreements (DPAs) with standard contractual clauses, state-of-the-art encryption at rest and in transit, and the necessity of transfer for the performance of our contract with you (Article 42).

